      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Windows paths lose the subject index used for fix routing",
      "description": "`extractFileIndex` gets the basename with `filePath.split('/')`. On Windows, paths produced by `path.join` use backslashes, so the newly added `subjectIndex` assignments that call this helper\u2014for example, for frontmatter-schema fixes\u2014can return `null` for indexed documents. Routing then treats the fix as having no index and falls back to the primary checkout, potentially writing the fix to the wrong checkout instead of the worktree that owns the document. Use a platform-aware basename operation and cover indexed-path routing with a Windows-style path test.",
